<title>HUNGARY: Hungary Sept net household savings rise HUF 18.9 b.</title>
<headline>Hungary Sept net household savings rise HUF 18.9 b.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1996-10-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Net household savings rose 18.9 billion forints in September to 2,227.7 billion forints, the National Bank of Hungary said on Thursday.</p>
<p>    (in billion forints) Sept 96    Aug 96    Sept 95</p>
<p> Forint savings	     2,108.6   2,090.9   1,654.2</p>
<p> Foreign currency	     471.0     469.6     411.3</p>
<p> Total savings		2,679.6   2,560.4   2,065.5</p>
<p> Total loans		    351.9     351.6     378.3</p>
<p> Net household savings    2,227.7   2,208.8   1,687.2</p>
<p>NOTE - Figures are not inflation adjusted. This year's figures are preliminary. The consumer price inflation was 22.2 percent year-on-year in September.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom(36 1) 327-4040</p>
</text>
